  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\n\nDry conditions are expected through at least the middle of the day on\nSaturday. Models are slightly faster in bringing rainfall into\nsouthern portions of the forecast area Saturday afternoon. Rain will\nthen overspread the region Saturday night into Sunday before starting\nto taper off Sunday evening. While the NBM keeps rainfall values\nranging from around a half inch to a little over an inch, there is\nthe potential for some locations to get over 2 inches of rain. There\nare multiple model solutions and ensembles showing the potential for\nthese localized higher values. Even with the potential for some \nlocations to get an inch and a half to over 2 inches of rain, the \nrain will be more steady instead of coming in a short duration. Due \nto this any flooding potential at this time looks to be more \nlocalized and lower end. Continued the trend from the previous shift\nto go 90th percentile NBM for wind gusts which allows for wind gusts\ngenerally around 25 to 35 mph. The higher wind gusts values would be\nSaturday evening.\n\nKey Message 2)\n\nDry conditions are expected for Monday. A weak system will bring some\nshowers to the area on Tuesday along with slightly cooler air for\nWednesday.",
